
userresources=$HOME/.Xresources
xinitdir="/etc/X11/xinit"

if [ -f "$userresources" ]
then
  xrdb -merge "$userresources"
fi

##
## Run all scripts in the `/etc/X11/xinit/xinitrc.d/` directory. This will set
## the necessary environment variables. These variables will be used by
## the `xdg-desktop-portal-gtk` service. This service, among other things, allows
## some applications (e. g. Firefox, Chromium, Electron applications) to display
## file picker dialogs in corresponding situations. Without setting the necessary
## environment variables the `xdg-desktop-portal-gtk` service will not start and
## some applications will not be able to display the file picker and other dialogs.
##
## Details
## -------
##
## ````
## ● xdg-desktop-portal is a system service on Linux that provides a
##   standardized way for sandboxed or confined applications (like Flatpak apps) to
##   access desktop features safely.
##
##   Its main purposes:
##
##    1. Sandboxing bridge — It acts as an intermediary between restricted apps
##       and the full desktop, allowing them to request access to sensitive resources
##       without having full system permissions.
##
##    2. Common access patterns — Provides a unified API for apps to:
##       - Open/save files (through native file dialogs)
##       - Print documents
##       - Access the clipboard
##       - Take screenshots
##       - Access camera/microphone
##       - Access location data
##       - And other desktop features
##
##    3. User control — The portal prompts users to approve requests, giving
##       them control over what permissions apps get (similar to mobile app permission
##       systems).
##
##    4. Cross-desktop compatibility — Works across different desktop
##       environments (GNOME, KDE, etc.) by using backend implementations specific to
##       each environment.
##
## Example: A Flatpak app can't directly access your file system, but it can use
## xdg-desktop-portal to ask permission to open a file, and the user sees a native
## file dialog.
##
## Claude Haiku 4.5
## ````
##
if [ -d "$xinitdir"/xinitrc.d ]
then
  for f in "$xinitdir/xinitrc.d"/?*.sh
  do
    [ -x "$f" ] && . "$f"
  done
  unset f
fi

exec openbox-session

